se,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-02-19T00:38:08Z","updated_at":"2026-05-30T10:11:34Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.6.stable.official\n- Reproducible in v4.6.1.stable.official\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.1.stable.mono - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9186) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-13700F (24 threads) - 15.84 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe AudioServer input mixrate will always be the same as the output mixrate. \nIf you change the sample rate of your microphone, the input mixrate will not change in godot.\nHowever, if you change the sample rate of your output, it will change both the input and output mixrate.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nRun any godot project and use theses lines to test the mixrate:\n`GD.Print(\"Input Mixrate: \" + AudioServer.GetInputMixRate());`\n`GD.Print(\"Output Mixrate: \" + AudioServer.GetMixRate());`\n\nTo change the mixrate of your output and input, go to your sound settings and change the default format.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116460/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116460/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}